---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../public/images/me1.jpg';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout className="home-main">
  <section class="founder-hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="founder-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Engineer · Researcher · Education</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Curiosity is not<br /><em>a privilege.</em></h1>
      <p class="founder-statement">
        It is how children learn — and it should not depend on what a family can afford.
      </p>
      <p class="founder-lede">
        I’m Pardeep Kumar. After more than a decade in engineering and research, I’m turning towards
        school education, and towards inquiry-led, curiosity-driven learning that ordinary families in
        India can actually reach.
      </p>
      <p class="founder-lede">
        I trained as an aerospace engineer at IIT Bombay and have spent my working life building
        software and doing research in India and the Netherlands. Mathematics, physics, and
        computation were the subjects that taught me how to learn. What I keep returning to is how
        much a single good question can change what a child understands.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button-link" href={`${base}what-i-believe/`}>What I believe about learning <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${base}my-story/`}>My story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-footnote"><span class="fine-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> I write here about the why. The rest takes shape in conversation.</div>
    </div>
    <figure class="founder-portrait">
      <div class="portrait-window">
        <Image src={portrait} alt="Portrait of Pardeep Kumar" widths={[480, 800, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 90vw, 40vw" width={900} format="webp" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
        <span class="portrait-index" aria-hidden="true">A NEW CHAPTER / EDUCATION</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption><span><strong>Pardeep Kumar</strong><br />Learning how to learn.</span><span class="portrait-sign" aria-hidden="true">PK</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="background-strip" aria-label="Background at a glance">
    <div class="shell background-strip-inner">
      <p>A foundation in<br /><strong>ideas &amp; execution</strong></p>
      <div><strong>10+ years</strong><span>Engineering &amp; research</span></div>
      <div><strong>IIT Bombay</strong><span>Aerospace engineering</span></div>
      <div><strong>CWI / TU Delft</strong><span>Doctoral research</span></div>
      <div><strong>India ↔ Europe</strong><span>A cross-border perspective</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-block shell chapter-grid" aria-labelledby="belief-title">
    <div class="section-label"><span>01 / WHY EDUCATION</span><span class="section-line"></span></div>
    <div class="chapter-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">The conviction</p>
      <h2 id="belief-title">A good education<br />should not depend<br />on <em>an accident of birth.</em></h2>
      <p>
        I went to school in a village and then in a small town, where the work was almost entirely
        rote. Living in the Netherlands since 2019 has made the gap plain: children here are taught
        to argue a point, work in a group, hold a room, lose a match, and notice where someone else’s
        boundary is — not as extras, but as part of what a school is for.
      </p>
      <p>
        I had to assemble most of that late, and in public. Inquiry-led learning and the skills a
        person actually lives by are not luxury features bolted onto schooling. They are the ordinary
        everyday work of helping a child learn how to learn, and they belong to every child.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${base}what-i-believe/`}>What I believe about learning <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <aside class="belief-card">
      <span class="belief-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      <p class="eyebrow">The starting point</p>
      <p class="belief-statement">Ask the question.<br />Sit with it.<br />Find out why.</p>
      <p>The habits that carried me through engineering and research are the same ones a ten-year-old can be taught.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="founder-background section-block" aria-labelledby="background-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-label"><span>02 / THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</span><span class="section-line"></span></div>
      <div class="background-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">From engineering to education</p>
          <h2 id="background-title">A builder’s mindset.<br /><em>A wider ambition.</em></h2>
          <a class="text-link" href={`${base}my-story/`}>Read my story <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="background-copy">
          <p>I trained in aerospace engineering at IIT Bombay and spent more than a decade working across software, engineering, and research in India and the Netherlands.</p>
          <p>My experience includes Shell, ASM International, and doctoral research at CWI Amsterdam and TU Delft. Along the way, I’ve built scientific software and independent digital products, taking ideas through to working systems.</p>
          <p>That experience shapes how I think about education: ask good questions, bring capable people together, and put care into the everyday execution.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="work-links">
        <a href={`${base}what-i-believe/`}><span>Beliefs</span><strong>How children learn</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${base}notes/`}><span>Notes</span><strong>Thinking out loud</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href={`${base}contact/`}><span>Contact</span><strong>Start a conversation</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-block shell connect-section" aria-labelledby="connect-title">
    <div class="section-label"><span>03 / LET’S TALK</span><span class="section-line"></span></div>
    <div class="connect-heading">
      <h2 id="connect-title">If any of this<br />sounds <em>familiar to you.</em></h2>
      <p>I’d like to hear from teachers, school leaders, parents, and anyone who thinks carefully about how children are taught.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
